      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/22/5212",
      "text": [
        ":\nسَأَلْتُ أَبَا جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ قَتَلَ رَجُلاً خَطَأً فِي أَشْهُرِ اَلْحُرُمِ قَالَ \"عَلَيْهِ اَلدِّيَةُ وَ صَوْمُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ مِنْ أَشْهُرِ اَلْحُرُمِ\" قُلْتُ إِنَّ هَذَا يَدْخُلُ فِيهِ اَلْعِيدُ وَ أَيَّامُ اَلتَّشْرِيقِ فَقَالَ \"يَصُومُهُ فَإِنَّهُ حَقٌّ لَزِمَهُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5212 - Ibn Mahbub narrated from Ali ibn Ri'ab from Zurarah, who said:\nI asked Abu Jafar Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) about a man who accidentally killed another man during the sacred months (Ashhur Al-Hurum).\nImam (as) said: \"He must pay the blood money (diyyah) and fast for two consecutive months from the sacred months.\"\nI said: \"But this period includes Eid and the days of Tashriq (the days following Eid Al-Adha).\"\nImam (as) replied: \"He must still fast them, for it is an obligation that has become binding upon him.\""
        ]
      }
    },
